# full-ai-cluster/k8s/bootstrap/k3s-packaged-manifest.skip
#
# A k3s SKIP MARKER. Its content is never read -- only its FILENAME matters, and
# the filename is set by `target` in `nixos/modules/k3s-server.nix`, which links
# this one file into /var/lib/rancher/k3s/server/manifests/ twice:
#
#   coredns.yaml.skip                     -> k3s ignores its packaged coredns.yaml
#   metrics-server-deployment.yaml.skip   -> k3s ignores its packaged metrics-server Deployment
#
# k3s pkg/deploy/controller.go `listFilesIn`: every `<name>.skip` in the tree
# makes the deploy controller ignore any manifest whose BASENAME is `<name>`.
# The replacements are `k3s-coredns.yaml` and `k3s-metrics-server.yaml` beside
# this file; their headers carry why (liveness probes that kill a slow-but-alive
# floor component under memory pressure, measured on dispatch 36119931377).
#
# Not `.yaml`, on purpose: the deploy controller only applies .yaml/.yml/.json,
# so this file is never itself submitted to the API server.
